## A new model, step by step (29 October 2026)

1. Folder : copy this folder to `<atelier>/lines/`, the scripts to `<atelier>/Scripts/lines/` ; set `ROOT` at the top of each script (one value per script). (29 October 2026)
2. Server : `Scripts/lines/ZrlServeRestart.sh` (port 8766), then open http://127.0.0.1:8766/3d.html in the built in browser. (29 October 2026)
3. Model : in the 3D editor, Source of truth, type the OBJ path (one `g` group per part) and press Use this model ; untick the 2D views when the object has no calibrated sheet yet. Or from the shell : `python -I Scripts/lines/ZrlUseModel.py --obj model.obj`. (29 October 2026)
4. Sheet : cut the six view sheet with SheetSplit.py and calibrate it with SheetFit.py (frame.json), then `python -I Scripts/lines/ZrlSheetViews.py --frame <frame.json> --panels <views dir>` ; the sheet then shows behind the model in the 3D editor and as the background of the 2D views. (29 October 2026)
5. Curves : New empty network, then Quad patch (A), Draw (D), Extend a strip (E), Insert edge loop (L) ; name the components (C, or Name faces from the model). (29 October 2026)
6. Check : Preview faces (P), N for each problem and its fix, Repair network, Bridge islands, Best pattern (B) or Best patterns for all faces. (29 October 2026)
7. Result : Convert to mesh (the preview is the result), Send to Houdini (`/obj/ZRL_Retopo`, one name per component), exports in `work/lines/exports`. (29 October 2026)
8. New version of the model : Use this model again ; every curve moves onto the new surface. `original` goes back to the validated car. (29 October 2026)

