## Components, chain and Houdini round trip (29 October 2026)

- Components panel : double click a name (or F2) to rename, + face to give a component one more face, iso, x to remove the name (Shift : with its own curves), filter ; Cmd Z undoes everything. (29 October 2026)
- Build chain in Houdini : `/obj/ZRL_Chain` is rebuilt from `work/lines/chain/chain_latest.json` : one NURBS curve of order 4 per curve (same knots as ZenRay Retopology), the quads and one COMP_ output per component. Move control points in `EDIT_curves`, then Pull curves from Houdini. (29 October 2026)
- The moment to switch : once the shape is validated against the reference sheet, the user's curves are the source of truth of the topology ; correct the curves, never the mesh. (29 October 2026)

## The app (29 October 2026)

- `scripts/lines/app/BuildLinesApp.sh` builds `~/Applications/ZenRay Meshes.app` : a launcher (no copy of the code) that starts or relaunches the server on port 8766 and opens `3d.html` in a Chrome app window with a private profile. `version-guard.js` reloads the page when its code changes (never over unsaved work) and relaunches the server when its Python changes. (29 October 2026)

## Click tools and the components view (29 October 2026)

- Auto patch (W) : click a zone, a four sided patch is fitted on its real contour (POST /auto_patch, ZrlAutoPatch.py), named from the Components field, mirrored ; a ring zone (tyre) comes as four quarters sharing their seams. (29 October 2026)
- Points snap to the mesh edges : a clicked point within 2 cm of a sharp edge or a part border goes onto it. (29 October 2026)
- Grey or Colours (Shift V) : one colour per part of the model ; Names (Shift N) : the name of each component in its middle, following the view, hidden behind other parts, never overlapping. (29 October 2026)
- Isolate a component (U, or the tool) : one part alone, framed, then draw on it ; U again or Shift H shows everything. (29 October 2026)
- Merge two points (Shift M) : two points of the curves become one node in their middle, on the surface ; the curves keep their shape ; mirror points too. (29 October 2026)

